{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789406464,"nonce":"N12S2oW91oxj6bpi1Sj7ljKLB1Q=","title":"Inner f64 body of a ternary-bodied recursive Num function fails the Cranelift verifier","message":"class F { static fib(n) { n \u003c 2 ? n : fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2) } }\n    System.print(F.fib(32))\n\nruns 0.7 s in the interpreter because the baseline compile fails and\nis never retried; the same function written with `if (n \u003c 2) return n`\ncompiles and runs in 13 ms. WLIFT_JIT_DEBUG=1 shows\n\n    COMPILE ERR FuncId(1): Verifier errors in inner wlift_fib___:\n      inst38 (jump block3(v35)): arg v35 has type f64, expected i64\n\nso the inner f64 body (the specialisation d4532dc restricted to\nself-recursive bodies) hands a raw f64 to a block parameter typed as a\nboxed Value: the ternary's merge block takes both arms as Values while\nthe arm that is the raw parameter `n` stays f64. With\n--jit-threshold 1 (no profile) the ordinary body compiles fine.\nEither the merge parameter should be typed f64 when every arm is, or\nthe arm should be boxed at the jump. Found 2026-09-14 while measuring\nisolates.","files":null}]}